      "message": "[From Jetski review] Bug (out-of-bounds read / UB): Previously this was guarded by `static_cast\u003cunsigned\u003e(elem) \u003e\u003d 0x80 ||`. Since `char` is signed on x86_64 Linux/Windows/macOS, removing that guard means non-ASCII bytes (`0x80..0xFF`) will sign-extend `static_cast\u003cint\u003e(elem)` to `-128..-1` and read before the start of `kShellValid`.\n\nPlease cast to `uint8_t` (or `unsigned char`), matching `EscapeStringToString_PosixNinjaFork`:\n\n```cpp\nif (!kShellValid[static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(elem)]) {\n```",
